e weight of it: proof that one person, in Edinburgh's Old Town, in any age, can tip the scales.\n\nthe old soldier visits with the children, who are told the story as a fairy tale — which, Thomas Beckett reflects, is what all true stories become, if they're lucky.\n\nthe blackmailer is a name in the records, a caution. Edinburgh's Old Town is a place where the mills run fair and the magistrate is honest, mostly, which is as much as any age can ask."}]}

